From c6dd45d978fd2b60a604a0ffbfab8cc94cc2849f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:29:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] egl/android: never hold DRM master

The swrast pass opens the PRIMARY node, and opening one makes the opener DRM
master whenever the device has no master yet (drm_master_open()). EGL is
initialised inside SurfaceFlinger and inside every app process, so one of them
wins that race against the compositor, which then cannot get it:

    drmhwc: DRM/KMS master access required
    drmhwc: No pipelines available. Creating null-display for headless mode

-- a console and no GUI, caused by the one process that had no business being
master. Observed as soon as kms_swrast started opening the primary node on an
NVIDIA Ada: every EGLImage failure was gone and the display went headless
instead.

kms_swrast wants this fd only for dumb buffers, and
DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB is declared with no flags at all (drm_ioctl.c:708),
so it needs no master. Only the compositor should hold it.

Dropping right after open is a no-op on render nodes and whenever we did not
become master -- it just returns an error, which is why the result is ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ghm63XPLUfxBs2tU2pnkjX
Change-Id: I02b2900b367d0f800f350b877d29b310f90be8ce
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c
index 7d53be98a3a..aa69ff19b63 100644
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c
@@ -1143,6 +1143,27 @@ droid_open_device(_EGLDisplay *disp, bool swrast)
          goto next;
       }
 
+      /* Never hold DRM master.
+       *
+       * The swrast pass opens the PRIMARY node, and opening one makes the
+       * opener master whenever the device has no master yet
+       * (drm_master_open()). EGL is initialised inside SurfaceFlinger and
+       * inside every app, so one of them wins that race against the
+       * compositor, which then cannot get it:
+       *
+       *     drmhwc: DRM/KMS master access required
+       *     drmhwc: No pipelines available. Creating null-display for headless
+       *
+       * -- a console and no GUI, from the one process that had no business
+       * being master. kms_swrast wants this fd only for dumb buffers, which
+       * DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB serves with no flags at all and therefore
+       * no master requirement. Only the compositor should hold it.
+       *
+       * A no-op on render nodes and whenever we did not become master, which
+       * is why the result is ignored.
+       */
+      drmDropMaster(dri2_dpy->fd_render_gpu);
+
       /* If a vendor is explicitly provided, we use only that.
        * Otherwise we fall-back the first device that is supported.
        */
-- 
